    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="5ce38317-3727-5810-99fe-d2e4f55dd8ab" activityNameId="dce84ca6-1956-5c4a-975b-2bcb28c68bd5" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xx Use, printer, laser jet, b/w, printing per h</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xx Use, printer, laser jet, b/w, printing per h
The laser jet printer use (b/w, office) is calculated according to the share between active (2 hrs/day), standby (7 hrs/day) and off (15 hrs/day) modes taken from literature information. The dataset includes the share of the printer production (assumed life span 4 years, running 240 days a year), the energy consumption for the different modes in the use-phase, the rail and road transport from factory to user, the paper and toner usage as well as the benzene emissions during 1 hour of printing.;
UUID: 3ab3c19f-2a69-3f28-82fb-361344d5b793
Describes the use of a laser jet printer (monochrome) in an office. Calculated per 1 hour of printing. Swiss supply mix applied for electricity consumption (low voltage).
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: No technology involved, except for the production of printer, LWC-paper and toner, which are represented in the individual subdatasets.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Manufacturers, literature and own assumptions. 
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: Assumptions had to be made for the printer life span.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_3ab3c19f-2a69-3f28-82fb-361344d5b793.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
